# VVDN -- REVISED COORDINATED 35L/35R OPERATIONS
# 3 arrivals land RWY 35L at planned 3-minute intervals; 3 departures use RWY 35R.
#
# Revision objectives:
#  1) The operational anchor is the START OF TAKE-OFF ROLL. VDN701/702/703
#     begin rolling at exactly 3-minute intervals. The first roll is triggered
#     30 s after VDN601 reaches touchdown altitude; later rolls are chained at
#     +180 s, so aircraft-type or arrival-path variation cannot erode the
#     departure interval.
#  2) Departure pushbacks are spaced 3 minutes (00:00 / 03:00 / 06:00), not
#     2 min 30 s. All aircraft taxi to the RWY 35R holding point at
#     16deg01min45.70secN / 108deg12min12.06secE
#     (16.029361,108.203350) and stop before entering the runway.
#  3) No aircraft occupies RWY 35R for several minutes. VDN701 lines up shortly
#     before the first slot; VDN702/703 enter at +120 s after the preceding roll
#     and are ready for their own roll at +180 s.
#  4) Arrivals that must cross RWY 35R stop at G4/G6. Crossing is released only
#     after the paired departure has passed 16.0574,108.1984 plus a 5 s buffer.
#  5) Taxi speeds are kept within a practical 10-15 kt range, with lower speed
#     near holding positions/gates. The revised holding point is approximately
#     108 m from the runway line-up point used in this simulation.
#
# IMPORTANT LIMITATION:
# The source file referenced internal PCALL files that were not attached. This
# revised package recreates those files. Arrival taxi paths after crossing RWY
# 35R are plausible schematic paths between the source coordinates and must be
# checked against the approved aerodrome ground-movement chart before use in a
# formal safety assessment.
#
# Planned timeline (approximate arrival touchdown; exact departure intervals):
#   VDN601 TD ~13:03  -> VDN701 roll ~13:33
#   VDN602 TD ~16:03  -> VDN702 roll exactly 3:00 after VDN701
#   VDN603 TD ~19:03  -> VDN703 roll exactly 3:00 after VDN702
#
# Callsigns are synthetic. This is a simulation scenario, not an operational
# clearance or approved procedure.

00:00:00.00>TRAILS ON
00:00:00.00>ASAS OFF

